schema.description:
Side-load request containing vector records to insert.

Example:
```json
{
    "records": [
        {
            "text": "This is sample text content",
            "vector": [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, ...],  // Optional: 1536-dimensional vector
            "metadata": {"source": "manual", "category": "test"},
            "document_id": "doc_001"  // Optional: will generate UUID if not provided
        },
        {
            "text": "Another piece of content",
            "metadata": {"source": "import", "priority": "high"}
            // vector and document_id will be auto-generated
        }
    ],
    "batch_size": 50
}
```

get.description:
Stream real-time progress updates for a PDF generation job using Server-Sent Events (SSE).

    This endpoint provides live progress updates as the PDF is being generated, without
    requiring polling. It uses Redis Pub/Sub to receive events from the ARQ worker,
    making it work seamlessly across Kubernetes pods.

    **Usage:**
    ```javascript
    const eventSource = new EventSource('/api/format/pdf-stream/abc-123');
    eventSource.addEventListener('progress', (event) => {
        const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
        console.log(`${data.progress}% - ${data.message}`);
        if (data.is_complete || data.is_error) {
            eventSource.close();
        }
    });
    ```

    The stream automatically closes when:
    - The job completes successfully (is_complete=true)
    - The job fails (is_error=true)
    - The client disconnects

    Returns:
        - 200: SSE stream of progress events
        - 403: Access denied (job belongs to different organization)
        - 404: Job not found

Retrieve detailed information about a specific cache entry using its cache key.
    This includes the original request, cached response, and metadata about the cache entry.

    The response includes:
    * Original request parameters
    * Cached response data
    * Cache metadata (creation time, TTL, expiration status)

    Example response:
    ```json
    {
        "cache_key": "abc123...",
        "request": {
            "query": "Show me the relationships between payment and vendor",
            "max_nodes": 20,
            "min_similarity": 0.3
        },
        "response": {
            "nodes": [...],
            "edges": [...],
            "metadata": {...},
            "summary": {...}
        },
        "metadata": {
            "created_at": 1234567890.123,
            "ttl_seconds": 3600,
            "ttl_remaining": 1800.5,
            "is_expired": false
        }
    }
    ```

post.description:
Set one or more cache entries using the same format as the dump endpoint.
    This allows you to easily copy-paste the output from /api/graph/cache/dump
    to restore or update cache entries.

    The request should match the format of the dump endpoint:
    ```json
    {
        "entries": [
            {
                "cache_key": "abc123...",
                "request": {
                    "query": "Show me the relationships between payment and vendor",
                    "max_nodes": 20,
                    "min_similarity": 0.3
                },
                "response": {
                    "nodes": [...],
                    "edges": [...],
                    "metadata": {...},
                    "summary": {...}
                },
                "metadata": {
                    "created_at": 1234567890.123,
                    "ttl_seconds": 3600,
                    "ttl_remaining": 1800.5,
                    "is_expired": false
                }
            }
        ]
    }
    ```

